#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("Disbelief Yeah, disbelief, it's Kufr not Shirk, Disbelief. This is.. this person has just cursed Allah and I congratulated him for cursing my God, do you understand how problematic that is? Why am I giving this analogy? Because this is effectively what happens Because Allahﷻ says in the authentic Hadith that شتَمَنِي ابنُ آدمَ Son of Adam has cursed me and then Allah explains that he ascribed to me a Son. What is the curse that he did? He ascribed to me a son وأنا اللَّهُ الأحدُ الصَّمدُ I'm The One Unique, Uniquely One الصمد The Independent So when he says الأحدُ الصَّمدُ because if you have a son that son is also God.", "الصَّمدُ The Self-Sufficient, The Independent so there's no one that depends.. Everyone depends on Allah alone, you cannot be depending on Jesus and Allah then you're not الصَّمدُ anymore, You're not the one that is Sufficient for the needs of all the Creation, so that's why Allah mentions الأحدُ الصَّمدُ, right! And Allah says شتَمني ابنُ آدمَ so Allah is telling you to ascribe a Son to Allah is cursing Allah Because initially, you are demeaning the status of Allah rather than saying he's One, Absolute, Self-Sufficient, you've ascribed a partner to Allah, and then a Muslim goes and he congratulates the person for cursing Allah, because effectively that's what the holiday is about, it is the celebration of the birth of the Son of God, and you have a Muslim who..", "congratulates another person. Muslims need to understand this is effectively what you're doing? Whether you understand or you don't understand, it's effectively what you're doing Or you're celebrating the association and the people who worship other than Allah and give sacrifices for other than Allah, so they can have good agriculture and good رزق (Rizq: Sustenance) and either way this is a problem of what you're doing And the fact that there are Christians or many Christians that believe that this is the date that the Son of God was born, this is enough for it to be.. even if the truth is it isn't, they still believe it, so you congratulating them for it, you're congratulating them for that belief",))
