// T ML282 165,166,167,168,169,170,171,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196,197,198,199,200,201,202,203,204,205,206,207,208,209,210 | The Muslim Lantern | dash: | cut:0
#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("And سُبْحَانَ ٱللَّٰهِ SubhanAllah (Praise God) you find.. the statement of.. Which is a completely clear statement SubhanAllah of Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Al’as where he said: مَنْ بَنَى بِبِلَادِ الْأَعَاجِمِ (Who's staying in the lands of the disbelievers وَصَنَعَ نَيْرُوزَهُمْ وَمِهْرَجَانَهُمْ Nayrouz and Mehrajan are just celebrations: he celebrated with them and gifted with them and did all of these things وَتَشَبَّهَ بِهِمْ حَتَّى يَمُوتَ وَهُوَ كَذَلِكَ and he dies in that state حُشِرَ مَعَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ he will be gathered with them on the Day of Judgment) This is a statement of a صحابي (Sahabi: a Companion of the Prophetﷺ) Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Al’as, this is not just your friend saying this He's saying this is what's going to happen and that's why..", "it's based on the Hadith of the Prophetﷺ من تشبَّهَ بقومٍ فَهوَ منْهم (Who imitates a group of people, he is from among them) Again some people \"oh you're being extreme\", brother I'm just telling you what the Prophetﷺ said you know. I just.. I'm reading to you what the Prophet is saying, what the Sahaba (Companions) are saying. It's not my opinion The Prophetﷺ said من تشبَّهَ بقومٍ فَهوَ منْهم. And Shaikh Al Islam Ibn Taymiyya, he commented on that, and he said: The least thing you can take from this Hadith is whoever does that, is committing a Major Sin, because if you take it as it’s apparent, the person is committing Disbelief.", "He's a Disbeliever because فَهوَ منْهم, he's from them! If you imitate Disbelievers you become? A Disbeliever! This is the least you could say is it's Haram you know The least you could say is this is Haram you know. The least! but there is no other options that you can go to. And that's why the Prophetﷺ when he went to Medina and he found out the people in Medina are celebrating different holidays that they had, people of.. the Kuffar (Disbelievers) of Quraish, and people who were living in Medina, the people.. those different people had certain holidays, when the Prophetﷺ he went to Medina as well the people of Medina had their own celebrations So the Prophetﷺ he said: what is all of this.", "They said: the holidays. So the Prophetﷺ he said: أما نحن (but us) we have 2 holidays: Eid Al-Adha and Eid Al-Fitr. He didn't say you know what, celebrate with them, gift with them, it's OK you know it's a fun time, you know, you can dance and have trees in the background. No! he said what? He said look \"but us\", so what is this? A separation, \"but us\", which means there's us and them now. It’s not a one group where everyone is doing the same mumbo jumbo, there's no such thing. \"But us\", meaning separation now, we have 2 holidays, we have Eid Al-Adha and Eid Al-Fitr.", "This is what we have as Muslims, these are the times in which you celebrate as a Muslim. Other than that, you don't go outside of this circle and what is -really- the reason those people celebrate? What is the real problem in the Muslim Ummah?",))
