#host("The Muslim Lantern", ("All of this, like.. All of this \"mumbo-jumbo\" that was going on from the beginning of the video is to reach this point: Mawlid The point of celebrating the Birthday of the Prophetﷺ. You have to do all of this like.. misrepresenting statements, Attributing things to people they didn't do, calling things which are instructions and buildings Bid'ah, You have to do all of this just to try to legitimise the action that you do which is celebrating the Birthday of the Prophetﷺ Honestly, you have to go through all of.. Do you see? Isn't this enough evidence for the people watching to know that this is something not from the religion?", "If it was from the religion, you'll easily find the Hadith, you'll easily find a statement from a Companion, a Companion doing it You'll go to that straight away and you'll save yourself time, but when you have to go in a circle like this, bring things that are not related, Make up statements and all of that, so you can just say \"Mawlid\", it is clear evidence that you've got no evidence, literally You're just making things up in order for you to push forward your agenda And then, he says that which \"agrees with the rules of the religion\"..", "Yeah, the rules of the religion say that every Bid'aah is misguided There cannot be a Bid'aah Hasana there, because the Prophetﷺ.. What did he say? He said every Bid'ah is misguidance.. [That's it!] So if it goes against.. If it's anything you innovate, then it's against the religion The Prophetﷺ said, \"There is nothing that brings you closer to Allahﷻ except that I've told you, and there is nothing that brings you closer to Hellfire except that I forbade you from\" So, if you tell us: \"this Mawlid -or whatever innovation you want to bring- it brings you closer to Allahﷻ\", then this opposes the Sharia, the religion..", "the statement that you just said. And if it doesn't bring you closer to Allahﷻ, then you are just bringing something into Islam and going against the tradition of the Prophetﷺ Where he said that you cannot bring anything into Islam. So those people who do the Mawlid believe that this is out of love for the Prophetﷺ And this brings you closer to Allahﷻ, but the Prophetﷺ himself already told you: \"There's nothing that brings you closer to Allah except that I've already told you\" And he says: مَنْ أَحْدَثَ فِي أَمْرِنَا هَذَا مَا لَيْسَ مِنْهُ فَهُوَ رَدٌّ (Whoever innovates anything in this religion that is not a part of it, then it's rejected) These are not my statements, brother.", "I don't need to go in a circle like you and like.. \"This building is an innovation\".. I don't need to do any of that. I can just tell you \"The Prophetﷺ said..\" You see, Islam is very simple, man. \"The Prophet ﷺ said..\" that's it.. Follow what the Prophetﷺ said and don't waste your time anymore. It's a very simple thing I'm going to talk a little bit about the \"Mawlid\" now. This idea, look.. The Mawlid of the Prophetﷺ.. If anyone celebrates the birthday of the Prophetﷺ and they want to say that this action brings you closer to Allah Or they want to say that this is a good thing, then they need to explain to us why the Prophetﷺ did not command it Why did the Prophetﷺ not do it?", "Why did the Prophetﷺ, the Sahaba of the Prophetﷺ, who you would agree with me They love the Prophetﷺ more than you, unless you say that you love the Prophet more than the Sahaba, Then you've got your own problems, I don't need to deal with you even.. So, if you say that the Sahaba -as you agree, and the Tabi'in and the Atba' Attabi'in, because they were the best of generations- They already loved the Prophetﷺ more than me and you or anyone else loves the Prophetﷺ That means that if this action was good and they love the Prophet more than you and me, then they would have done it But you don't have the Sahaba or the Tabi'in or Atba' Attabi'in, or the year after it or the year after it or the year after Until we came to the فاطميين (Fatimids) hundreds and hundreds and hundreds of years later", "Where a group of people decided to innovate this idea of celebrating the birthday of the Prophetﷺ Some of them will tell you, \"No, the Prophetﷺ celebrated his birthday. He did man, but you just don't know!\" OK, when did the Prophetﷺ celebrate his birthday? They will say to you that the Prophetﷺ fasted Monday and he said, \"This is the day I was born in.\" Let me tell you the trickery here and the funny trickery about this idea. The Prophetﷺ when he fasted.. If I want to accept their claim, \"The Prophetﷺ fasted Monday because he was born Monday\"..", "Did the Prophetﷺ fast the date that he was born? This is what a birthday is. You celebrate ربيع الأول Rabi' al-Awwal Rabi' al-Awwal can come on a Wednesday, Friday, Saturday, Sunday, it can come any day It doesn't have to be a Monday because it's a specific date. So, when you say that you celebrate a birthday, you're not celebrating Monday, are you? Why are you not celebrating Monday then? You should be celebrating Monday because the Prophetﷺ fasted Monday So when he says \"the day I was born in\", he's referring to Monday, he's not referring to the date, which is 12 Rabi' al-Awwal He was not looking at the calendar when it is 12 Rabi' al-Awwal and celebrating that day Let's say I'm born on a Friday.", "That Friday has a specific date in the calendar If I celebrate the specific date, sometimes it's going to be Friday, sometimes it's going to be Saturday, sometimes it's going to be Sunday This is a birthday, but to celebrate Friday itself as a day, then this is a different story now So they misattribute things to the Prophetﷺ of Allah and they say he celebrated his birthday. That was not his birthday That was Monday, a specific day and the Prophetﷺ did not say \"just because I was born in it\", he said he fasted for a specific reason He said he fasted Monday because: \"this is a day I was born on, it is a day I'm going to die and it is a day that I was..", "بُعِثت فيه.. given Messenger-hood in\" Because all of these events happened on a Monday, so the Prophet decided to fast on a Monday And Thursday because the deeds are uplifted to Allah, so he wants his deeds -when they're lifted to Allah- that his deeds are lifted when he's fasting So, he's saying -because of all of these events happening on a specific day- I'm fasting that day He's not saying, \"Celebrate my birthday, celebrate 12 Rabi' al-Awwal\" -which by the way- there's no evidence that this is the time that he was born You even have people who say, \"OK, you can celebrate the birthday..", "And they themselves tell you that we do not know when he was born exactly How are you going to celebrate his birthday when you don't even know when he was born? SubhanAllah, people will try to do anything for the sake of their own.. They want to play music and dance and celebrate and do all of this stuff That's why they will play with the religion, try to make up things to say, \"We should celebrate it, it's a part of Islam\" Let's finish this video",))
